  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Trials, groups, and research that exist",
   "text": "According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a trial of a medicine called JR-446 for MPS IIIB is currently recruiting, with sites in Germany, the United Kingdom, and the United States [Eaba71d6, E78c4e47, E8b3818d, E84ae8d7]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, another JR-446 trial for MPS IIIB in Japan is active but not currently recruiting [Eeb73a12, E4266ba7, E4fcb0b9]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a trial of a medicine called Tralesinidase alfa given into the fluid around the brain for MPS IIIB is listed as not yet recruiting [E77f7e53, E5905aee], and the same medicine is also available through a separate early access program [E88775fa, Ec16392e]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a gene therapy trial using rAAV9-CMV-hNAGLUop for MPS IIIB in the United States is not yet recruiting [E2d2fc39, E88ddde1, E4e0c623]. According to NIH RePORTER, NIH NINDS funds a grant working on a NAGLU gene therapy vector that studies MPS IIIB [Ef6abcfe, E1d51bde], and NIH NCATS funds a grant using patient stem cell-derived models that also studies MPS IIIB [Ea480d65, E0b4a14c]. Several patient groups around the world say they support families with MPS IIIB, including groups in Canada, Italy, Spain, the United States, Australia, and the Netherlands [E6941bc4, E994105e, Eeb45010, Ea7a71e3, Ed536e8b, E7fe60f3]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a related gene transfer trial called UX111 for MPS IIIA is recruiting in Australia, Spain, and the United States [Eebc4df2, Eb3c0db6, E4164417, E5dbae4a].",
